Jahshaka patch 0057 — a cascade added AFTER bounces were enabled must not break
the bounce shader.

SOURCE patch. EVERY TREE MUST RE-RUN `irisgl/scripts/build-ogre.sh` after
pulling this. It overlaps patches 0037 and 0050 in
`Components/Hlms/Pbs/src/Vct/OgreVctLighting.cpp` (different functions); they
apply in stack order, and a per-patch reverse-check on a tree that already
carries 0037/0050 reports this one "unapplied" for that file — judge by content
(CLAUDE.md, the overlap blind spot).

THE DEFECT, measured (lane PATCHES-1 / GI-REENABLE-1, 2026-09-15;
spikes/patches-1/gi-probe2.log). Enabling Photon's cascade chain raised, EVERY
time, on a fresh enable and on a re-enable:

    OGRE EXCEPTION(3:RenderingAPIException): Fragment Program
    34LightVctBounceInject_cs failed to compile … 'ogre_t6' : unrecognized
    layout identifier

and left `giStatus.vctBound = false` / `ifdBound = false`: the whole VCT arm
dead, no GI in the picture, and nothing but that one line in the engine log to
say so.

THE CAUSE. `runBounce()` sets `hlms_num_vct_cascades` from
`mExtraCascades.size() + 1` on every injection, and the generated compute shader
declares one light-voxel texture per cascade (four per cascade with anisotropy).
The job's TEXTURE UNIT COUNT and its bindings, though, are only ever derived in
`setupBounceTextures()` — which upstream calls from `setAllowMultipleBounces()`
and from `resetTexturesFromBuildRelative()`, and from nowhere else. So a caller
that enables bounces and THEN chains the inner cascades (`reserveExtraCascades`
+ `addCascade`) leaves the property saying "N cascades" while the root layout
still holds the six units of a chain of one: the shader references `ogre_t6`,
which does not exist, and the program never compiles.

Nothing in `VctLighting`'s header documents an order for those calls, and
upstream's own `VctCascadedVoxelizer` happens to chain BEFORE it enables bounces
(`OgreVctCascadedVoxelizer.cpp:449-458`), which is the only reason upstream
never meets this. `addCascade()` now re-derives the job when bounces are on, so
either order works — three lines where the alternative was an undocumented
ordering contract every caller has to know.

KNOWN RESIDUAL, recorded rather than fixed here: "VCT/LightVctBounceInject" is
found BY NAME, so every `VctLighting` in the process shares ONE
`HlmsComputeJob`, while the property is per-injection and the bindings belong to
whichever instance called `setupBounceTextures()` last — the same shared-job
class as patch 0037's defect 2. Two cascade chains alive at once (two scenes
with Photon cascades) would therefore inject one chain's voxels through the
other's textures. Jahshaka binds VCT process-wide to one scene
(`sVctBindingOwner`), so it is not reachable today; the robust fix is to
re-assert the bindings per dispatch in `runBounce()`, which upstream should
weigh against the per-iteration samplerblock reference-counting it does under
GL.

VERIFICATION. `git apply --check` on a tree carrying 0001-0056 and `git apply
--reverse --check` after applying; `build-ogre.sh` re-run in the lane worktree;
`--engine-selftest` byte-identical
(`b55e2d5d03dce4059b71a65f8e61dc4773fb0b048e3de05428aca83cabae0ec7`) — the
default scene runs no cascade chain. BEFORE/AFTER on the rig: the probe script
`spikes/patches-1/p1-gi-probe2.js` (fourteen GI flips, `app.engineErrors`
sampled after each) reports 1 recorded engine error on each cascade enable
before the patch and 0 after, with `vctBound` true. The suite is
`gi.reenable` (tests/gi/test_gi_reenable.cpp).

--- a/Components/Hlms/Pbs/src/Vct/OgreVctLighting.cpp
+++ b/Components/Hlms/Pbs/src/Vct/OgreVctLighting.cpp
@@ -839,7 +839,28 @@
         mExtraCascades.reserve( numExtraCascades );
     }
     //-------------------------------------------------------------------------
-    void VctLighting::addCascade( VctLighting *cascade ) { mExtraCascades.push_back( cascade ); }
+    void VctLighting::addCascade( VctLighting *cascade )
+    {
+        mExtraCascades.push_back( cascade );
+
+        // THE CHAIN DECIDES HOW MANY TEXTURES THE BOUNCE SHADER DECLARES, so the job has
+        // to be told the moment the chain grows. runBounce() sets
+        // hlms_num_vct_cascades from mExtraCascades.size() + 1 on every injection, and
+        // the generated compute shader declares one light-voxel texture per cascade
+        // (four with anisotropy) — but the job's TEXTURE UNIT COUNT and its bindings are
+        // only ever derived in setupBounceTextures(), which upstream calls from
+        // setAllowMultipleBounces() and resetTexturesFromBuildRelative(). Add a cascade
+        // after enabling bounces and the shader asks for ogre_t6 while the root layout
+        // still has six units: "'ogre_t6': unrecognized layout identifier", the compute
+        // program fails to compile, and the whole VctLighting arm renders no GI at all
+        // with nothing but that one log line to say so.
+        //
+        // Nothing documents an order for these two calls (VctLighting's header does not),
+        // and upstream's own VctCascadedVoxelizer happens to chain BEFORE it enables
+        // bounces, which is why upstream never meets this. Now either order works.
+        if( getAllowMultipleBounces() )
+            setupBounceTextures();
+    }
     //-------------------------------------------------------------------------
     void VctLighting::setAllowMultipleBounces( bool bAllowMultipleBounces )
     {
